(1) status/refresh/reload load the config themselves to find listen + admin token, so while the file on disk is invalid they die in their own startup and never reach the daemon (seen in the 2026-09-21 smoke test: 'Invalid configuration at hub.bogus_key ... at lib/MCP/Hub.pm line 340.'). The daemon-side refusal via POST /_hub/reload works. Decide: accept, or let --url + explicit token bypass config loading. (2) Config::_err croaks, and Carp appends 'at FILE line N.' even with a trailing newline; reload strips it at its boundary, startup and CLI do not. (3) 'mcp-hub refresh' prints 'NAME 0 tools' for an unbuildable entry, which reads as success.
